1
00:01:05,795 --> 00:01:07,213
Good morning.

2
00:01:07,297 --> 00:01:08,464
Good morning.

3
00:01:08,548 --> 00:01:09,799
Nice weather today.

4
00:01:09,883 --> 00:01:11,092
It's so hot out.

5
00:01:11,176 --> 00:01:12,385
Yeah.

6
00:01:16,347 --> 00:01:19,184
TALKING PLUSHIE - WANPAKU
HELLO WOOF!

7
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:28,276
We're with the police.

8
00:01:28,359 --> 00:01:31,070
Is your boss, Mr. Tadashi Yazu, here?

9
00:01:32,155 --> 00:01:33,156
What?

10
00:01:34,032 --> 00:01:35,241
Kousuke.

11
00:01:36,784 --> 00:01:38,244
Are they customers?

12
00:01:38,328 --> 00:01:39,954
You must be Mr. Tadashi Yazu.

13
00:01:40,038 --> 00:01:41,372
Huh? Yes, I am.

14
00:01:41,456 --> 00:01:45,001
We would like to ask you
about the plushie manufactured here.

15
00:01:45,710 --> 00:01:48,171
-Can you come with us?
-Huh?

16
00:01:48,254 --> 00:01:49,839
What is this about?

17
00:01:49,923 --> 00:01:52,008
We'll share the details later.

18
00:01:52,091 --> 00:01:53,509
Explain it to me!

19
00:01:53,593 --> 00:01:56,596
We will talk it over at the station.

20
00:01:56,679 --> 00:01:58,556
Hold on a second!

21
00:02:14,197 --> 00:02:16,407
JUSTICE'S FORM

22
00:02:19,285 --> 00:02:21,621
MIYUKI SHIRAMOTO
BORN 1981, KANAGAWA

23
00:02:23,081 --> 00:02:24,457
Why…

24
00:02:25,917 --> 00:02:29,837
LET'S EXPERIENCE A MOCK TRIAL!

25
00:02:29,921 --> 00:02:32,548
TRIAL OBSERVATION PROGRAM PARTICIPANT

26
00:02:41,015 --> 00:02:43,226
You're full of energy this morning.

27
00:02:43,309 --> 00:02:45,019
Good morning.

28
00:02:45,103 --> 00:02:47,772
I have to go to
Mr. Uramawashi's place now.

29
00:02:47,855 --> 00:02:49,107
Oh, I see.

30
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:51,693
I have to watch him closely,
so he doesn't mess up.

31
00:02:51,776 --> 00:02:53,027
Again?

32
00:02:55,446 --> 00:02:57,949
How long do I have to keep doing this?

33
00:03:00,576 --> 00:03:01,703
Good morning.

34
00:03:01,786 --> 00:03:03,663
-Morning.
-Good morning, Ms. Aso.

35
00:03:03,746 --> 00:03:06,499
This just went on sale today!
Vanilla Hoji Tea Latte.

36
00:03:06,582 --> 00:03:08,418
I bought it for you. Here you go!

37
00:03:08,501 --> 00:03:10,211
I don't do sugar this early.

38
00:03:11,129 --> 00:03:12,005
Rejected!

39
00:03:12,088 --> 00:03:16,092
<i>The popular talking plushie, Wanpaku,</i>
<i>is under suspicion of being illegally sold</i>

40
00:03:16,175 --> 00:03:19,804
<i>to overseas terrorist groups,</i>
<i>to be used as a weapon.</i>

41
00:03:19,887 --> 00:03:21,889
<i>The President of Yazu Works,</i>
<i>Mr. Tadashi Yazu</i>…

42
00:03:21,973 --> 00:03:24,517
Terrorism with a plushie?

43
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:25,893
How scary!

44
00:03:25,977 --> 00:03:27,729
Agreed.

45
00:03:27,812 --> 00:03:29,772
How about a regular coffee?

46
00:03:29,856 --> 00:03:31,107
No need.

47
00:03:32,233 --> 00:03:34,360
-I'll have it.
-I'm not giving it to you.

48
00:03:34,444 --> 00:03:35,486
Come in.

49
00:03:36,487 --> 00:03:37,697
Good morning.

50
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:39,198
You're late.

51
00:03:40,491 --> 00:03:47,415
This is Ms. Aso, a brilliant lawyer who
will be handling your father's defense.

52
00:03:47,498 --> 00:03:48,416
Huh?

53
00:03:50,626 --> 00:03:52,086
Nice to meet you!

54
00:03:54,213 --> 00:03:57,050
<i>Hello, woof! Let's get along, woof!</i>

55
00:03:57,133 --> 00:03:58,343
Huh?

56
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:16,652
Yazu Works was originally
a small town factory that made sensors.

57
00:04:16,736 --> 00:04:19,530
Then the President, Mr. Tadashi Yazu,
used those sensors

58
00:04:19,614 --> 00:04:22,116
to create a talking plushie
that reacts to people's faces.

59
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:24,494
The Wanpaku. It was an instant hit.

60
00:04:27,789 --> 00:04:30,416
<i>Hello, woof! I'm Wanpaku, woof!</i>

61
00:04:31,167 --> 00:04:33,961
There's even merchandise.
It's very popular among the youth.

62
00:04:34,045 --> 00:04:36,089
Getting arrested over a plushie …

63
00:04:36,172 --> 00:04:38,132
Are the police even serious?

64
00:04:38,216 --> 00:04:40,968
If they weren't,
they wouldn't have arrested him.

65
00:04:41,052 --> 00:04:43,763
Plus, they weren't regular cops,
but Public Security.

66
00:04:43,846 --> 00:04:46,265
They specialize in spies and terrorists.

67
00:04:46,349 --> 00:04:50,186
I guess they don't want Japan's
advanced tech to be leaked overseas.

68
00:04:50,269 --> 00:04:53,773
So our little boy here caught
the attention of guys like that.

69
00:04:53,856 --> 00:04:55,983
The police are bad news.

70
00:04:56,067 --> 00:04:58,736
I think we shouldn't get involved.

71
00:05:00,530 --> 00:05:01,489
What?

72
00:05:02,073 --> 00:05:04,117
Mr. Kureta? It's the police!

73
00:05:06,077 --> 00:05:10,915
Why did you take the job just to foist it
on me, Mr. Uramawashi?

74
00:05:11,457 --> 00:05:17,088
In World War II, the Church of Our Lady
in Dresden endured two days of bombing,

75
00:05:18,297 --> 00:05:20,341
but when people were evacuating,

76
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:22,635
it collapsed.

77
00:05:23,261 --> 00:05:24,512
Excuse me?

78
00:05:24,595 --> 00:05:25,721
Are you listening?

79
00:05:33,187 --> 00:05:34,647
Miss,

80
00:05:35,273 --> 00:05:37,316
our company doesn't make weapons!

81
00:05:37,942 --> 00:05:40,069
No matter what I say, they keep saying,

82
00:05:40,153 --> 00:05:43,072
"You knew it would be used
as a weapon, admit it."

83
00:05:43,948 --> 00:05:46,951
Who would ever think
of using a stuffed animal as a weapon?

84
00:05:47,034 --> 00:05:49,203
I'm begging you, please believe me.

85
00:05:50,580 --> 00:05:52,748
The Wanpaku is our treasure.

86
00:05:53,875 --> 00:05:57,545
We didn't design it to explode
in response to the sensor!

87
00:05:58,838 --> 00:06:01,674
I understand.
I will investigate this thoroughly.

88
00:06:02,675 --> 00:06:04,135
Thank you very much.

89
00:06:04,635 --> 00:06:08,014
The police have suspected you
from the very beginning,

90
00:06:08,097 --> 00:06:11,017
so their investigation may be biased.

91
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:14,687
It must be painful, but no matter
what they say, don't admit guilt…

92
00:06:14,770 --> 00:06:16,397
You must remain silent.

93
00:06:17,023 --> 00:06:17,857
What?

94
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:20,484
You never know
what they will do to trick you.

95
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:24,947
If you confess, we can't win anymore.

96
00:06:26,532 --> 00:06:28,367
So maintain absolute silence.

97
00:06:28,451 --> 00:06:30,453
Yes, I understand.

98
00:06:30,536 --> 00:06:31,871
Hold on, Mr. Uramawashi…

99
00:06:31,954 --> 00:06:33,247
Well then, excuse me.

100
00:06:41,839 --> 00:06:43,216
My apologies.

101
00:06:47,136 --> 00:06:48,679
It's just as you see.

102
00:06:50,181 --> 00:06:53,142
This is the result.
We can't even run the factory.

103
00:06:55,478 --> 00:06:59,023
Well, it's not like
we have any orders now.

104
00:07:03,194 --> 00:07:06,113
Will my father be released soon?

105
00:07:07,490 --> 00:07:10,117
Are they still suspecting us?

106
00:07:12,036 --> 00:07:14,163
I think the police intend to investigate

107
00:07:14,247 --> 00:07:16,791
until the last moment
of the detention period.

108
00:07:16,874 --> 00:07:18,668
But it's going to be okay.

109
00:07:18,751 --> 00:07:21,629
You didn't do anything wrong.

110
00:07:23,130 --> 00:07:24,048
Yes.

111
00:07:24,131 --> 00:07:27,927
Once the suspicion is cleared,
I'm sure you'll get tons of orders again.

112
00:07:29,679 --> 00:07:32,390
I really hope so.

113
00:07:34,058 --> 00:07:37,270
<i>Welcome, woof! Nice to woof you!</i>

114
00:07:38,771 --> 00:07:41,315
Sorry. We arrived ahead of schedule.

115
00:07:41,399 --> 00:07:45,319
It's okay. Ms. Aso, this is Mr. Isogai.

116
00:07:46,112 --> 00:07:49,824
I am Aso, the lawyer handling
Mr. Yazu's case.

117
00:07:50,658 --> 00:07:54,245
I am Shinichiro Isogai
from Isogai Corporation.

118
00:07:57,123 --> 00:08:00,084
Cordia! That's a major firm.

119
00:08:01,335 --> 00:08:05,339
Ms. Aso, please take good care of Mr Yazu.

120
00:08:05,423 --> 00:08:07,883
-Please protect the Wanpaku.
-Mr. Isogai!

121
00:08:07,967 --> 00:08:09,218
Please get up!

122
00:08:09,802 --> 00:08:11,679
Sorry, I instinctively…

123
00:08:13,014 --> 00:08:16,225
Is Mr. Yazu doing all right?
Have you visited him?

124
00:08:16,851 --> 00:08:19,145
ISOGAI CORPORATION CEO
SHINICHIRO ISOGAI

125
00:08:24,317 --> 00:08:26,485
Oh, it's Ms. Aso.

126
00:08:27,069 --> 00:08:30,197
Mr. Kureta? Why are you here?

127
00:08:30,281 --> 00:08:34,035
Just watching the boat race over there.
Let's go.

128
00:08:34,118 --> 00:08:35,661
What do you mean, "Let's go"?

129
00:08:35,745 --> 00:08:38,289
-Come on.
-No, I want to go over there.

130
00:08:38,372 --> 00:08:39,707
You head back first.

131
00:08:39,790 --> 00:08:40,625
Yes.

132
00:08:53,137 --> 00:08:54,805
What is going on?

133
00:08:55,431 --> 00:08:57,933
Keep calm and listen to me.

134
00:08:58,017 --> 00:08:59,644
I feel like…

135
00:09:00,645 --> 00:09:02,104
We are being followed.

136
00:09:02,188 --> 00:09:04,523
-Huh?
-Well, just to be safe.

137
00:09:05,066 --> 00:09:07,777
Hey, wait! The station is that way!

138
00:09:07,860 --> 00:09:09,320
-Let's cross the bridge.
-No!

139
00:09:12,531 --> 00:09:14,033
Who is following us?

140
00:09:14,116 --> 00:09:17,078
Who else could be tailing us but…

141
00:09:17,161 --> 00:09:19,080
Wait, Public Security?

142
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:27,129
Hey!

143
00:09:42,895 --> 00:09:45,690
Is it that person over there?

144
00:09:49,193 --> 00:09:50,903
It's so hot, jeez.

145
00:10:17,972 --> 00:10:20,433
Huh?

146
00:10:20,516 --> 00:10:21,934
What?

147
00:10:31,402 --> 00:10:34,071
Which way did they go…

148
00:10:34,947 --> 00:10:36,031
This way?

149
00:10:43,998 --> 00:10:44,915
Followed?

150
00:10:44,999 --> 00:10:46,834
That's what Mr. Kureta claimed.

151
00:10:46,917 --> 00:10:50,963
I know they suspect Mr. Yazu,
but isn't tailing me a bit too much?

152
00:10:51,589 --> 00:10:54,383
Maybe there's something
they don't want us to know.

153
00:10:55,092 --> 00:11:00,473
The way I see it,
Yazu Works is an honest, loving company.

154
00:11:02,349 --> 00:11:05,352
The CEO of Isogai also came
because he was worried.

155
00:11:06,479 --> 00:11:07,688
Out of the way.

156
00:11:07,772 --> 00:11:10,441
Isogai develops industrial robots,

157
00:11:10,524 --> 00:11:12,943
and is featured
in the next Super Tech Expo.

158
00:11:13,652 --> 00:11:14,862
I made an appointment.

159
00:11:14,945 --> 00:11:18,240
I wanted an opinion on the Wanpaku
from a different perspective.

160
00:11:18,324 --> 00:11:24,747
So, Mr. Uramawashi,
please continue being a good architect.

161
00:11:40,888 --> 00:11:42,556
<i>Get to work, woof!</i>

162
00:12:00,282 --> 00:12:03,285
BRINGING ISOGAI'S TECH TO THE WORLD

163
00:12:03,369 --> 00:12:06,997
WELCOME TO THE GUIDED TOUR!

164
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:25,516
I am Aso from Cordia Law Firm.

165
00:12:30,938 --> 00:12:33,774
Well then, the tour is about to begin!

166
00:12:33,857 --> 00:12:35,276
Okay!

167
00:12:35,359 --> 00:12:36,735
Follow me.

168
00:12:42,992 --> 00:12:44,451
You must be Ms. Aso.

169
00:12:45,119 --> 00:12:46,870
I'm Takayama, executive assistant.

170
00:12:46,954 --> 00:12:48,747
-My card.
-Thank you very much.

171
00:12:48,831 --> 00:12:50,291
I'll show you around.

172
00:12:56,422 --> 00:12:58,757
<i>Everyone, this way, please.</i>

173
00:13:09,018 --> 00:13:11,312
PRESIDENT'S OFFICE
SECRETARY'S OFFICE

174
00:13:12,187 --> 00:13:13,188
This way.

175
00:13:13,856 --> 00:13:17,568
Mr. Isogai will be back shortly,
so please take a seat and wait.

176
00:13:21,196 --> 00:13:22,615
-Sakurai.
-Yes?

177
00:13:22,698 --> 00:13:24,700
The copier check-up
got changed to Thursday.

178
00:13:24,783 --> 00:13:26,035
Oh, got it.

179
00:13:26,118 --> 00:13:29,538
It's noon, so I'm going
to take my break first.

180
00:13:41,383 --> 00:13:43,552
Ms. Aso, I'm so sorry I'm late.

181
00:13:43,636 --> 00:13:44,678
Not at all.

182
00:13:47,723 --> 00:13:51,477
<i>Starting voice authentication.</i>
<i>What is today's weather?</i>

183
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:52,353
Sunny.

184
00:13:53,228 --> 00:13:56,482
<i>Where is the 2026 World Cup being held?</i>

185
00:13:56,565 --> 00:13:58,567
United States, Canada, Mexico.

186
00:13:59,485 --> 00:14:00,736
PRESIDENT'S OFFICE

187
00:14:00,819 --> 00:14:02,571
-Go ahead.
-Sir!

188
00:14:02,655 --> 00:14:06,617
The Expo Promotion Office sent an email,
they need you to check something.

189
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:08,077
Got it.

190
00:14:09,828 --> 00:14:10,704
Excuse me.

191
00:14:10,788 --> 00:14:14,249
Sorry. Let me take a look at the email.

192
00:14:20,381 --> 00:14:22,383
AUTHENTICATE WITH FINGERPRINT
FINGERPRINT VERIFIED

193
00:14:24,051 --> 00:14:26,887
Sorry to keep you waiting. Have a seat!

194
00:14:30,849 --> 00:14:33,435
You want to talk about Mr. Yazu, right?

195
00:14:35,229 --> 00:14:38,148
If there's anything I can do, let me know.

196
00:14:39,608 --> 00:14:41,652
Mr. Isogai, why do you care so much?

197
00:14:43,278 --> 00:14:46,699
We were originally a toy company.

198
00:14:47,282 --> 00:14:50,828
So, when I think about
how Mr. Yazu must feel,

199
00:14:50,911 --> 00:14:52,705
I just can't stand by and watch.

200
00:14:53,914 --> 00:14:58,877
The very first thing Isogai Co. made
was actually this little wind-up toy.

201
00:14:58,961 --> 00:15:01,797
From there, it overcame challenges
and grew into a company

202
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:04,925
that delivers technology
from Japan to the world.

203
00:15:05,009 --> 00:15:06,677
I see.

204
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:11,390
<i>We are thinking of moving forward</i>
<i>with a capital alliance with Yazu Works.</i>

205
00:15:11,473 --> 00:15:14,768
<i>Do you mean an acquisition?</i>

206
00:15:14,852 --> 00:15:15,811
What?!

207
00:15:15,894 --> 00:15:16,937
Is something wrong?

208
00:15:17,021 --> 00:15:18,856
-Oh!
-No…

209
00:15:18,939 --> 00:15:20,357
Please continue.

210
00:15:21,358 --> 00:15:22,359
Look this way.

211
00:15:22,443 --> 00:15:23,777
It hurts!

212
00:15:23,861 --> 00:15:27,698
This is our conclusion, after thinking
of a way to protect the Wanpaku.

213
00:15:28,949 --> 00:15:31,201
The Wanpaku is amazing.

214
00:15:31,827 --> 00:15:35,205
It recognizes people's faces
with outstanding speed,

215
00:15:35,289 --> 00:15:38,292
it makes you feel
like you're really conversing with it.

216
00:15:39,251 --> 00:15:40,461
This, too,

217
00:15:40,544 --> 00:15:44,798
is possible because Mr. Yazu refined
his technology without compromise.

218
00:15:46,008 --> 00:15:48,469
Losing everything
over a strange suspicion…

219
00:15:48,552 --> 00:15:50,637
That can't be allowed to happen.

220
00:15:53,557 --> 00:15:56,560
To be willing to take on
the debt to protect it…

221
00:15:57,102 --> 00:15:58,937
How admirable.

222
00:15:59,605 --> 00:16:02,441
You love stuff like that.

223
00:16:03,358 --> 00:16:04,276
No, this is bad.

224
00:16:04,359 --> 00:16:06,487
-Are you actually crying?
-Don't film it!

225
00:16:06,570 --> 00:16:09,531
-You're actually crying! How passionate
-Don't film me!

226
00:16:09,615 --> 00:16:10,657
Don't film me! Oh my!

227
00:16:11,325 --> 00:16:14,995
<i>-Intruders detected.</i>
-We were found out!

228
00:16:15,079 --> 00:16:17,581
-<i>Intruders detected.</i>
-We're sorry!

229
00:16:19,041 --> 00:16:21,293
My apologies!

230
00:16:21,376 --> 00:16:24,713
I will now guide you to the next room.

231
00:16:24,797 --> 00:16:26,799
This way, please.

232
00:16:52,157 --> 00:16:54,660
Kousuke! This is terrible!

233
00:16:54,743 --> 00:16:55,744
What happened?

234
00:16:55,828 --> 00:16:56,995
Look at this.

235
00:16:57,621 --> 00:17:01,041
THE MOMENT THE WANPAKU EXPLODED

236
00:17:20,727 --> 00:17:23,939
<i>Welcome, woof! Nice to meet you, woof!</i>

237
00:17:25,482 --> 00:17:26,441
Yes.

238
00:17:26,525 --> 00:17:28,902
My apologies for the trouble caused!

239
00:17:30,195 --> 00:17:31,238
I'm sorry.

240
00:17:31,905 --> 00:17:32,990
Excuse me.

241
00:17:33,615 --> 00:17:34,449
Mr. Yazu.

242
00:17:38,370 --> 00:17:42,916
That video, we don't even know its source.
It has no credibility whatsoever!

243
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:44,960
It doesn't matter.

244
00:17:45,460 --> 00:17:48,130
A toy made to bring joy to children…

245
00:17:48,922 --> 00:17:51,049
ended up hurting a child.

246
00:17:52,259 --> 00:17:54,761
That video is going viral.

247
00:18:01,310 --> 00:18:04,855
Just now, the bank told us
they are cutting off our loans.

248
00:18:04,938 --> 00:18:07,107
They said we have
to repay them right away too.

249
00:18:09,985 --> 00:18:13,822
Our clients also said they are returning
all of their inventory.

250
00:18:16,325 --> 00:18:18,243
Nobody believes we are innocent.

251
00:18:20,454 --> 00:18:23,248
I will request a payment deferral
from the bank.

252
00:18:24,041 --> 00:18:26,752
I believe you are innocent. So--

253
00:18:26,835 --> 00:18:28,045
That's enough, miss.

254
00:18:32,299 --> 00:18:36,094
It looks like Isogai
will be acquiring Yazu Works.

255
00:18:36,678 --> 00:18:39,348
I wanted to at least be of some help,

256
00:18:39,431 --> 00:18:43,268
so I'll help them draft
the business transfer agreement.

257
00:18:44,561 --> 00:18:46,688
You don't look satisfied with this.

258
00:18:48,273 --> 00:18:51,860
There's no way they actually
want to sell the company.

259
00:18:52,819 --> 00:18:54,488
Even with the Wanpaku case,

260
00:18:54,571 --> 00:18:57,824
they were willing to at least try
uncovering the truth.

261
00:18:57,908 --> 00:18:59,785
But then, because of that video…

262
00:19:00,452 --> 00:19:01,787
Humans…

263
00:19:02,788 --> 00:19:04,164
are creatures that lie.

264
00:19:04,248 --> 00:19:05,666
Lie?

265
00:19:05,749 --> 00:19:08,001
-Are you saying someone is lying?
-But…

266
00:19:09,711 --> 00:19:11,797
Space does not lie.

267
00:19:13,590 --> 00:19:15,342
What are you talking about?

268
00:19:16,009 --> 00:19:17,344
Isn't it amazing?

269
00:19:17,427 --> 00:19:20,347
Isogai wants to work with us.

270
00:19:24,559 --> 00:19:26,311
Are you fine with this?

271
00:19:29,439 --> 00:19:30,524
Obviously…

272
00:19:34,695 --> 00:19:37,990
it's better to make things
at a major company.

273
00:19:40,367 --> 00:19:41,868
The Wanpaku

274
00:19:44,538 --> 00:19:46,415
is already a thing of the past.

275
00:19:50,711 --> 00:19:51,920
True.

276
00:20:05,017 --> 00:20:10,188
At the Expo, we should be able to unveil
more advanced drones and security robots.

277
00:20:10,939 --> 00:20:12,899
This is thanks to all of you.

278
00:20:14,192 --> 00:20:17,612
Isogai's technology will eventually be
used by the police too,

279
00:20:17,696 --> 00:20:20,699
becoming a great force
protecting this country.

280
00:20:23,035 --> 00:20:26,163
To make that a reality,
we will assist in any way we can.

281
00:20:33,795 --> 00:20:35,714
COMPLETE GUIDE TO CONTRACT DRAFTING

282
00:20:54,316 --> 00:20:55,567
JUSTICE'S FORM

283
00:21:02,199 --> 00:21:07,079
A lawyer has to be
the client's biggest ally.

284
00:21:08,538 --> 00:21:11,375
No matter what,
you believe in them until the end,

285
00:21:11,458 --> 00:21:13,543
and fight for their sake.

286
00:21:14,628 --> 00:21:18,507
Otherwise,
how could they trust you to defend them?

287
00:22:45,510 --> 00:22:47,470
Beyond this perspective,

288
00:22:49,055 --> 00:22:51,016
the lie will reveal itself.

289
00:22:55,145 --> 00:22:57,355
Ms. Konno, can you prepare the costumes?

290
00:22:57,439 --> 00:22:59,774
I can't make good ones
at such short notice.

291
00:22:59,858 --> 00:23:02,652
You are very detail-oriented.

292
00:23:04,029 --> 00:23:06,948
Can I really do this?

293
00:23:07,032 --> 00:23:09,701
That's a heavy responsibility, Nakazaki.

294
00:23:11,536 --> 00:23:12,704
Man…

295
00:23:13,747 --> 00:23:15,373
I see.

296
00:23:15,457 --> 00:23:18,126
Looks fine.
That contract is very you, Yukari.

297
00:23:18,627 --> 00:23:19,753
I wish you luck.

298
00:23:20,378 --> 00:23:23,131
I will do all I can. See you.

299
00:23:23,215 --> 00:23:24,382
Take care.

300
00:23:41,358 --> 00:23:43,610
Sir, right this way.

301
00:23:43,693 --> 00:23:44,819
Huh?

302
00:23:44,903 --> 00:23:46,821
They have the same car?

303
00:23:46,905 --> 00:23:48,615
It seems so. Here you go, sir.

304
00:23:48,698 --> 00:23:50,951
Thank you. All right.

305
00:24:02,254 --> 00:24:03,755
Everyone, are you ready?

306
00:24:06,549 --> 00:24:10,136
Of course. All good.

307
00:24:13,390 --> 00:24:14,808
<i>There's no doubt</i>

308
00:24:14,891 --> 00:24:18,228
Isogai is pulling the strings
behind Public Security.

309
00:24:18,728 --> 00:24:20,981
<i>We'll obtain evidence</i>
<i>from the President's Office.</i>

310
00:24:21,064 --> 00:24:22,649
<i>We'll remake the lie.</i>

311
00:24:22,732 --> 00:24:24,150
<i>-Asuka.</i>
-Yes.

312
00:24:24,234 --> 00:24:25,402
<i>It's almost time.</i>

313
00:24:25,485 --> 00:24:26,945
There they are.

314
00:24:33,743 --> 00:24:36,079
-I'm so sorry!
-What?!

315
00:24:36,871 --> 00:24:38,456
-We have to clean it right away!
-Huh?

316
00:24:38,540 --> 00:24:40,375
-Let's go!
-Hold on…

317
00:24:42,168 --> 00:24:43,837
Take it off.

318
00:24:44,796 --> 00:24:46,715
-I happened to have this.
-Okay.

319
00:24:46,798 --> 00:24:49,217
Please wipe your skirt with it.

320
00:24:49,301 --> 00:24:50,552
I'll clean the jacket.

321
00:24:50,635 --> 00:24:52,429
Thank you.

322
00:24:54,681 --> 00:24:56,474
Oh, it's coming right off!

323
00:24:56,558 --> 00:24:57,684
Nakazaki.

324
00:24:57,767 --> 00:24:59,185
<i>How are things on your end?</i>

325
00:25:00,562 --> 00:25:01,813
Ms. Aso is here.

326
00:25:03,231 --> 00:25:06,609
Mr. Nakazaki? Why are you here?

327
00:25:06,693 --> 00:25:10,155
I was told to attend
today's contract signing for my studies.

328
00:25:10,238 --> 00:25:12,449
Mr. Uramawashi…

329
00:25:13,283 --> 00:25:15,910
Studies? But this is an important--

330
00:25:15,994 --> 00:25:18,288
Please, make an exception!

331
00:25:18,371 --> 00:25:20,081
What?

332
00:25:20,165 --> 00:25:21,750
<i>I am so sorry!</i>

333
00:25:21,833 --> 00:25:25,086
-It's fine.
-We cleaned it off nicely.

334
00:25:25,170 --> 00:25:26,504
Thank you very much.

335
00:25:26,588 --> 00:25:28,590
-I'm glad.
-Excuse me.

336
00:25:33,511 --> 00:25:34,512
A mistake?

337
00:25:34,596 --> 00:25:37,057
No, we actually received
an order for ten people.

338
00:25:37,849 --> 00:25:40,769
This puts me in a bind.
Please check one more time.

339
00:25:40,852 --> 00:25:44,022
I'm sorry. I was the one who ordered that.

340
00:25:44,606 --> 00:25:47,233
Oh, that's a relief.

341
00:25:47,317 --> 00:25:50,278
It's a lot of food,
so I'll deliver it inside for you.

342
00:25:50,362 --> 00:25:51,571
Thank you.

343
00:26:29,025 --> 00:26:32,445
Please be really quiet, okay?

344
00:26:32,529 --> 00:26:35,907
Of course. I'm good at reading the room.

345
00:26:36,408 --> 00:26:38,535
I'm kind of anxious.

346
00:26:39,536 --> 00:26:42,539
<i>Welcome, woof! Nice to meet you, woof!</i>

347
00:27:04,394 --> 00:27:06,271
Excuse me.

348
00:27:08,648 --> 00:27:11,693
-Who are you?
-I'm Hashimoto from General Affairs.

349
00:27:11,776 --> 00:27:14,279
We're handing these
out to all departments,

350
00:27:14,362 --> 00:27:16,656
so please share it with everyone.

351
00:27:16,739 --> 00:27:18,950
Oh, really?

352
00:27:19,784 --> 00:27:22,412
Could it be you are Mr. Takayama?

353
00:27:22,495 --> 00:27:23,788
I am.

354
00:27:23,872 --> 00:27:27,792
I heard from Sakurai that
you collect Obungu merchandise.

355
00:27:28,543 --> 00:27:29,794
Look at this.

356
00:27:29,878 --> 00:27:32,172
Actually, I love them too!

357
00:27:32,255 --> 00:27:36,009
I heard if you go by 1:00 p.m.,
you can get a limited edition item.

358
00:27:36,092 --> 00:27:38,970
Really? My daughter absolutely loves them.

359
00:27:39,053 --> 00:27:40,472
Thank you!

360
00:27:50,398 --> 00:27:52,442
There's somewhere I absolutely have to go!

361
00:27:52,525 --> 00:27:55,320
The President is away anyway!
I'll be back soon!

362
00:28:05,622 --> 00:28:07,832
All right, come on.

363
00:28:08,458 --> 00:28:11,377
You could have carried it
for me, you know.

364
00:28:11,461 --> 00:28:15,423
-You keep saying that--
-I'm always the one carrying stuff!

365
00:28:15,507 --> 00:28:16,883
Why is it always me…

366
00:28:16,966 --> 00:28:18,468
-Hello.
-Hello.

367
00:28:18,551 --> 00:28:20,595
We've come for the copier check-up.

368
00:28:22,514 --> 00:28:23,723
-Go ahead.
-Thank you.

369
00:28:23,806 --> 00:28:24,766
Thank you.

370
00:28:28,978 --> 00:28:31,314
I'll keep watch in case
the secretary comes back.

371
00:28:31,397 --> 00:28:33,233
Please do.

372
00:28:43,535 --> 00:28:44,577
This way.

373
00:28:50,250 --> 00:28:54,003
<i>Starting voice authentication.</i>
<i>What is today's weather?</i>

374
00:28:56,506 --> 00:28:58,925
<i>Nakazaki, time for you to shine.</i>

375
00:28:59,592 --> 00:29:01,010
Now?

376
00:29:01,845 --> 00:29:05,723
These are the conditions from Yazu Works.

377
00:29:07,684 --> 00:29:09,310
<i>Hurry, Nakazaki.</i>

378
00:29:14,858 --> 00:29:16,025
Hey!

379
00:29:17,735 --> 00:29:19,696
Do you think it will rain today?

380
00:29:19,779 --> 00:29:22,866
Hey! My apologies.

381
00:29:25,243 --> 00:29:26,995
Mr. Nakazaki, what is wrong with you?

382
00:29:27,078 --> 00:29:28,746
It might rain on the way back.

383
00:29:28,830 --> 00:29:31,332
But you don't have to ask now!

384
00:29:31,416 --> 00:29:34,669
Well, I think it will be sunny.

385
00:29:35,295 --> 00:29:37,839
No, that's not it.

386
00:29:38,923 --> 00:29:40,884
Sir, what do you think?

387
00:29:40,967 --> 00:29:41,801
Mr. Nakazaki!

388
00:29:41,885 --> 00:29:44,387
Oh, I agree with Mr. Yazu.

389
00:29:44,470 --> 00:29:46,472
Then, do you think it will be sunny?

390
00:29:46,556 --> 00:29:47,599
Mr. Nakazaki!

391
00:29:49,142 --> 00:29:51,769
Yeah, it will be sunny.

392
00:29:54,939 --> 00:29:58,443
<i>Keep up the good work.</i>
<i>Get him to answer the other one too.</i>

393
00:29:59,068 --> 00:30:01,946
<i>What kind of dance do robots hate?</i>

394
00:30:02,030 --> 00:30:03,114
Huh?

395
00:30:04,282 --> 00:30:06,576
What is that? Do robots even dance?

396
00:30:06,659 --> 00:30:07,994
It's a riddle.

397
00:30:08,578 --> 00:30:09,579
<i>Breakdance.</i>

398
00:30:09,662 --> 00:30:12,498
Because machines don't want to break down.

399
00:30:12,582 --> 00:30:15,084
Mr. Uramawashi is pretty good
at riddles too.

400
00:30:15,168 --> 00:30:17,879
Hey, do you know what kind
of dance robots dislike?

401
00:30:18,838 --> 00:30:20,465
<i>Hey, don't ask him directly!</i>

402
00:30:20,548 --> 00:30:23,384
You promised to read the room!

403
00:30:23,968 --> 00:30:27,555
I bet he's just trying
to lighten the mood.

404
00:30:28,806 --> 00:30:29,807
Yes.

405
00:30:34,187 --> 00:30:35,396
Breakdance?

406
00:30:36,230 --> 00:30:37,190
Is that it?

407
00:30:37,273 --> 00:30:38,316
Right.

408
00:30:38,399 --> 00:30:39,359
I see.

409
00:30:40,360 --> 00:30:42,278
I wasn't asking you, Mr. Yazu!

410
00:30:43,154 --> 00:30:44,113
Sir!

411
00:30:44,739 --> 00:30:46,407
Didn't you get your answer?

412
00:30:46,491 --> 00:30:47,867
Please, tell me the answer!

413
00:30:50,662 --> 00:30:51,621
Breakdance.

414
00:30:54,624 --> 00:30:56,751
Nakazaki, well done.

415
00:30:56,834 --> 00:30:58,127
Oh, wow.

416
00:30:58,211 --> 00:30:59,796
I see.

417
00:30:59,879 --> 00:31:01,255
I feel so relieved.

418
00:31:02,382 --> 00:31:03,591
Yeah.

419
00:31:06,636 --> 00:31:09,389
Well then, shall we continue
with the contract?

420
00:31:13,768 --> 00:31:16,020
Why's this guy--

421
00:31:24,904 --> 00:31:27,198
Come on, don't scare me like that.

422
00:31:41,045 --> 00:31:42,547
COPYING DATA

423
00:31:42,630 --> 00:31:45,341
Five minutes? That's quite a while.

424
00:31:54,017 --> 00:31:56,728
It keeps spinning around…

425
00:31:56,811 --> 00:31:58,187
Huh?

426
00:31:58,271 --> 00:32:01,357
I bet you need lots of improvements,
little guy.

427
00:32:03,401 --> 00:32:05,236
-Hey!
<i>-Intruders detected.</i>

428
00:32:05,319 --> 00:32:07,947
<i>-</i>What are you doing?
-I'm sorry! What do we do?

429
00:32:08,031 --> 00:32:11,492
-Just make it stop!
-You need a security guard's ID!

430
00:32:11,576 --> 00:32:14,078
<i>-Really?</i>
-<i>Intruders detected.</i>

431
00:32:14,162 --> 00:32:15,788
What do we do?

432
00:32:15,872 --> 00:32:17,832
<i>Intruders detected!</i>

433
00:32:19,459 --> 00:32:20,877
President's office. Hurry!

434
00:32:20,960 --> 00:32:22,086
Yes!

435
00:32:22,170 --> 00:32:24,630
The guards are coming!
I bet it sent a notification!

436
00:32:24,714 --> 00:32:26,299
Mr. Kureta, how much time left?

437
00:32:26,382 --> 00:32:29,677
Two, no, three minutes. Seriously?

438
00:32:29,761 --> 00:32:32,055
-It came from the President's office!
-Yes!

439
00:32:34,348 --> 00:32:36,434
Be quiet, please!

440
00:32:36,517 --> 00:32:38,686
-Be quiet!
-How do we turn it off?

441
00:32:38,770 --> 00:32:41,147
Please! Just finish already!

442
00:32:41,898 --> 00:32:43,566
How much time left?

443
00:32:43,649 --> 00:32:45,401
-Two minutes.
<i>-Intruders detected…</i>

444
00:32:45,485 --> 00:32:47,111
-You're so annoying!
<i>-Intruders…</i>

445
00:32:48,738 --> 00:32:50,448
We're at the president's office.

446
00:33:08,424 --> 00:33:09,592
Mr. Yazu?

447
00:33:14,263 --> 00:33:18,768
THE TALKING PLUSHIE, WANPAKU

448
00:33:31,447 --> 00:33:35,159
I look forward to our future endeavors.

449
00:33:36,744 --> 00:33:37,995
Of course.

450
00:33:53,511 --> 00:33:56,013
<i>Intruders detected.</i>

451
00:33:57,098 --> 00:34:01,561
<i>Intruders detected.</i>

452
00:34:01,644 --> 00:34:03,020
Another malfunction?

453
00:34:07,692 --> 00:34:09,193
Just to be safe, check around.

454
00:34:09,277 --> 00:34:10,236
Yes, sir!

455
00:34:10,319 --> 00:34:12,238
-We'll go this way.
-Yes, sir!

456
00:34:21,539 --> 00:34:23,249
We've recovered the USB.

457
00:34:28,462 --> 00:34:30,214
Good work, everyone.

458
00:34:33,467 --> 00:34:36,762
Has the contract been finalized?

459
00:34:37,430 --> 00:34:42,018
Yes, fortunately.
We can make it in time for the Expo.

460
00:34:46,772 --> 00:34:47,982
Wait.

461
00:35:00,244 --> 00:35:01,829
What is this photo?

462
00:35:03,456 --> 00:35:04,582
Photo?

463
00:35:15,218 --> 00:35:17,220
You're making a scary face.

464
00:35:17,803 --> 00:35:20,139
The contract was successfully signed,
wasn't it?

465
00:35:20,223 --> 00:35:21,307
Yes.

466
00:35:21,390 --> 00:35:24,769
However, the suspicions
against Mr. Tadashi haven't been cleared.

467
00:35:24,852 --> 00:35:27,146
True.

468
00:35:27,230 --> 00:35:29,440
Ms. Tsunehiro,
take care of these documents.

469
00:35:29,523 --> 00:35:30,441
Yes.

470
00:35:35,488 --> 00:35:36,572
Huh?

471
00:35:42,995 --> 00:35:45,373
Space does not lie.

472
00:35:48,376 --> 00:35:50,211
This is…

473
00:35:52,046 --> 00:35:53,506
MR. URAMAWASHI

474
00:35:57,093 --> 00:35:57,927
Yes.

475
00:35:59,136 --> 00:36:02,974
POLICE HEADQUARTERS

476
00:37:35,191 --> 00:37:42,198
CABARET CLUB PURPLE

477
00:38:10,101 --> 00:38:13,312
<i>I've been waiting for you, woof.</i>
<i>Welcome, woof.</i>

478
00:38:15,398 --> 00:38:17,691
Sorry for making you wait.

479
00:38:18,275 --> 00:38:20,277
Public Security Chief Matoba.

480
00:38:20,361 --> 00:38:23,656
Mr. Uramawashi, this is not a good way
to ask people things!

481
00:38:24,740 --> 00:38:26,742
What kind of stunt is this?

482
00:38:27,410 --> 00:38:28,536
Ridiculous.

483
00:38:41,340 --> 00:38:42,591
What is the meaning of this?

484
00:38:52,643 --> 00:38:53,477
What?

485
00:38:55,271 --> 00:38:58,441
Public Security drove Yazu Works
into a corner.

486
00:38:59,233 --> 00:39:01,444
Isogai Corp bought it up.

487
00:39:02,236 --> 00:39:04,071
And then the Expo.

488
00:39:05,364 --> 00:39:09,660
The pillars that seemed separate
were actually connected by a beam.

489
00:39:10,661 --> 00:39:14,915
In order to showcase
Isogai's security robots to the world.

490
00:39:15,708 --> 00:39:16,584
Huh?

491
00:39:18,669 --> 00:39:21,589
The security robots' program data.

492
00:39:23,048 --> 00:39:25,801
Before the talk of an acquisition
even came up…

493
00:39:26,510 --> 00:39:29,638
Yazu's sensor technology
was already built into it.

494
00:39:29,722 --> 00:39:30,556
What?

495
00:39:30,639 --> 00:39:32,516
What are you talking about?

496
00:39:33,392 --> 00:39:36,145
So, in order to obtain Yazu's technology,

497
00:39:36,228 --> 00:39:38,981
they had Public Security
plant evidence and arrest Yazu?

498
00:39:39,064 --> 00:39:40,441
Correct.

499
00:39:41,609 --> 00:39:43,736
What kind of joke is this?

500
00:39:43,819 --> 00:39:46,322
How do you plan to explain
that overseas video?

501
00:39:46,405 --> 00:39:49,158
That is what the next question is for.

502
00:39:52,995 --> 00:39:53,913
Huh?

503
00:39:55,956 --> 00:39:59,627
This video doesn't feel like
it was shot overseas.

504
00:40:00,586 --> 00:40:02,463
That outlet is the Japanese standard.

505
00:40:02,546 --> 00:40:05,508
And this is the 24-hour ventilation system
unique to Japan.

506
00:40:05,591 --> 00:40:10,012
Also, this window is a horizontal
sliding aluminum sash, common in Japan.

507
00:40:10,095 --> 00:40:11,263
In other words,

508
00:40:11,805 --> 00:40:15,309
this room looks foreign,
but it is not foreign architecture.

509
00:40:15,392 --> 00:40:18,395
This footage was shot in Japan.

510
00:40:19,063 --> 00:40:21,023
Very well done.

511
00:40:21,106 --> 00:40:22,775
Even if that were true,

512
00:40:22,858 --> 00:40:25,653
this footage has no connection
to us whatsoever.

513
00:40:26,779 --> 00:40:30,407
Do you think this is the only evidence
we've obtained?

514
00:40:32,785 --> 00:40:36,330
The footage showing
the making of this video

515
00:40:37,289 --> 00:40:39,500
was left behind at Isogai Corp.

516
00:40:42,878 --> 00:40:48,759
Shall I show you
the moment your lies crumble?

517
00:40:58,185 --> 00:40:59,228
Enough already!

518
00:41:04,441 --> 00:41:05,693
Aso.

519
00:41:11,657 --> 00:41:12,908
Mr. Yazu…

520
00:41:13,450 --> 00:41:15,536
Please release him, without charges.

521
00:41:18,497 --> 00:41:19,748
Very well.

522
00:41:20,583 --> 00:41:24,878
No matter what you say now,
the acquisition is already complete.

523
00:41:27,590 --> 00:41:28,716
I wonder.

524
00:41:37,349 --> 00:41:39,184
Why was the acquisition canceled?

525
00:41:39,268 --> 00:41:41,228
<i>It's because of that lawyer woman.</i>

526
00:41:42,021 --> 00:41:45,274
These are the conditions from Yazu Works.

527
00:41:48,652 --> 00:41:52,072
If Yazu's innocence is proven
by the execution of the business transfer,

528
00:41:52,156 --> 00:41:54,199
this contract will be null and void.

529
00:41:54,283 --> 00:41:57,453
Furthermore, if our company
was involved in the incident,

530
00:41:57,536 --> 00:42:00,456
the loaned operating capital
will also be waived.

531
00:42:00,956 --> 00:42:03,208
That lawyer!

532
00:42:09,340 --> 00:42:11,008
<i>I'm sorry, woof.</i>

533
00:42:16,347 --> 00:42:20,267
Mr. Yazu was released due to
insufficient evidence, with no indictment.

534
00:42:20,351 --> 00:42:22,478
I'm glad we worked hard.

535
00:42:22,561 --> 00:42:26,565
People are saying that the video
looks fake, AI-generated.

536
00:42:26,649 --> 00:42:28,776
I hope the Wanpaku's popularity returns.

537
00:42:28,859 --> 00:42:30,027
I think it will.

538
00:42:30,110 --> 00:42:31,654
They have more capital now,

539
00:42:31,737 --> 00:42:34,406
so maybe they can make
an even more amazing one.

540
00:42:35,741 --> 00:42:37,951
Ms. Aso is incredible.

541
00:42:41,830 --> 00:42:43,791
When did you realize it?

542
00:42:45,250 --> 00:42:47,336
Whoa, you're sharp.

543
00:42:48,337 --> 00:42:51,090
You also know that this lighting
is Louis Kahn's style?

544
00:42:51,173 --> 00:42:54,718
I didn't mean that. How did you know
the Expo was involved?

545
00:42:55,803 --> 00:42:59,306
I simply used a different approach
than the one you took.

546
00:43:00,391 --> 00:43:04,061
I kept quiet back then,
but where was that photo taken?

547
00:43:04,144 --> 00:43:07,231
How did you get the program data?
Did you plot something again?

548
00:43:07,314 --> 00:43:11,068
If you know,
you'll become an accomplice too.

549
00:43:13,278 --> 00:43:16,031
No way. I'm not helping a liar like you!

550
00:43:16,115 --> 00:43:17,074
That's a shame.

551
00:43:17,908 --> 00:43:20,077
I really can't stand you!

552
00:43:21,578 --> 00:43:25,165
The one who protected Yazu was you, Aso.

553
00:43:26,083 --> 00:43:27,459
<i>Thank you, woof!</i>

554
00:43:28,669 --> 00:43:29,503
Look.

555
00:43:29,586 --> 00:43:30,921
Isn't it great?

556
00:43:32,339 --> 00:43:36,427
When it comes from you, Mr. Uramawashi,
it all sounds like a lie!

557
00:43:36,510 --> 00:43:37,636
Excuse me.

558
00:43:47,062 --> 00:43:49,523
We are thinking it would be great
if we could build

559
00:43:49,606 --> 00:43:52,234
the Expo's main venue,
the Future Pavilion, there.

560
00:43:52,317 --> 00:43:53,986
In that venue,

561
00:43:54,069 --> 00:43:57,156
we will display Japan's amazing robot tech
and next-gen mobility!

562
00:43:57,239 --> 00:44:00,659
If a giant pavilion is built at the center
of the Expo venue,

563
00:44:00,743 --> 00:44:03,370
and Japan's cutting-edge technology
is shown there,

564
00:44:03,454 --> 00:44:06,206
it will surely become a hot topic
all over the world.

565
00:44:06,290 --> 00:44:10,794
Well, Japanese robot tech is top-class,
that much is true.

566
00:44:10,878 --> 00:44:14,548
I'll also have to work hard
so your robots don't take my job.

567
00:44:15,466 --> 00:44:17,801
-Surely you're joking!
-No, I mean it.

568
00:44:17,885 --> 00:44:19,887
Well then, that will be all for today.

569
00:44:19,970 --> 00:44:21,597
Looking forward to our partnership!

570
00:44:21,680 --> 00:44:23,557
-Thank you very much.
-Excuse us.

571
00:44:32,483 --> 00:44:36,278
I hear Isogai Corp is preparing
for the Expo. How are they doing?

572
00:44:36,361 --> 00:44:37,404
About that,

573
00:44:37,488 --> 00:44:40,282
I heard they failed to buy
a small-town factory,

574
00:44:40,365 --> 00:44:42,493
and couldn't get their sensor tech.

575
00:44:42,576 --> 00:44:44,119
What do you mean?

576
00:44:44,203 --> 00:44:48,415
A female lawyer hired by the factory
performed beyond expectations.

577
00:44:49,124 --> 00:44:50,959
Is that so?

578
00:44:52,419 --> 00:44:53,921
I went to the trouble

579
00:44:54,963 --> 00:44:58,050
of recommending Isogai Corp
as a key enterprise for the Expo,

580
00:44:58,133 --> 00:44:59,635
yet it failed.

581
00:45:01,512 --> 00:45:02,679
I understand.

582
00:45:04,139 --> 00:45:05,474
By the way,

583
00:45:07,601 --> 00:45:11,438
who is that female lawyer
you talked about?

584
00:45:14,274 --> 00:45:15,275
I see.

585
00:45:15,943 --> 00:45:18,403
How wonderful, you were able to save them.

586
00:45:18,987 --> 00:45:20,030
Well…

587
00:45:20,113 --> 00:45:22,950
I can't say I used a good method.

588
00:45:23,033 --> 00:45:25,118
That Church of Our Lady in Dresden.

589
00:45:25,202 --> 00:45:28,372
It has been rebuilt and now stands
as a symbol of peace.

590
00:45:28,455 --> 00:45:31,959
I wonder, was he betting on the Wanpaku?

591
00:45:32,042 --> 00:45:35,420
Did he believe in the Wanpaku
from the very beginning?

592
00:45:35,504 --> 00:45:37,464
No, maybe I'm overthinking it.

593
00:45:39,299 --> 00:45:41,635
He's a really unusual lawyer.

594
00:45:47,307 --> 00:45:49,184
<i>We have not engaged in any exam fraud.</i>

595
00:45:49,268 --> 00:45:52,312
<i>I can't forgive the university</i>
<i>that stole my daughter's dream.</i>

596
00:45:52,396 --> 00:45:53,939
<i>Someone is trying to frame me…</i>

597
00:45:54,022 --> 00:45:56,483
<i>They must have left evidence behind.</i>

598
00:45:56,567 --> 00:46:00,445
She resembles you. She also cannot leave
vulnerable people alone.

599
00:46:00,529 --> 00:46:02,864
<i>The way you do things is wrong.</i>

600
00:46:02,948 --> 00:46:05,325
<i>Some people can't be saved</i>
<i>through legal means alone.</i>

601
00:46:05,409 --> 00:46:06,827
<i>It was you, wasn't it?</i>

602
00:46:07,494 --> 00:46:08,453
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

